Phase 1: Refresh Algorithmic Thinking
1. Grokking Algorithms, 2nd Edition

Author: Aditya Bhargava
 Level: Beginner Refresh
 Time: 2 to 3 weeks
 Priority: Optional for an experienced developer

This is the easiest starting point if DSA has not been part of your regular work for several years. It uses visual explanations for binary search, recursion, sorting, hash tables, breadth-first search, Dijkstra’s algorithm, greedy techniques, and dynamic programming. Contemporary recommendations continue to position it as an accessible starting point rather than a complete interview-preparation resource.

Read selectively

Focus on:

Big-O notation
Binary search
Recursion
Quicksort
Hash tables
Breadth-first search
Dijkstra’s algorithm
Greedy algorithms
Dynamic programming
Skip this book if

You can already:

Calculate time and space complexity
Implement binary search without a template
Explain recursion and the call stack
Traverse trees and graphs
Solve easy array and hash-map problems comfortably
Practical milestone

Implement in Java:

Binary search
Merge sort
Quicksort
Breadth-first search
Depth-first search
Dijkstra’s algorithm
LRU cache

Do not use library shortcuts during the first implementation.

